[tool_result] toolu_015wTfUcFbT25bTGCCxMnzCN 1	# Phase 4 decision memo — drill config + scoring refinement
2	
3	(Supersedes the Phase 3 memo. Prior memos preserved in git history.)
4	
5	## Goal
6	Make the engine configurable on a per-profile basis, tighten scoring so
7	that "late" is an explicit, configurable threshold (not a side effect of
8	the response window), surface a per-cue breakdown the athlete can act on,
9	and add an anti-rhythm signal so the user can spot rhythm-anticipation
10	patterns before competition.
11	
12	## Phase 4 acceptance criteria (unchanged from `docs/PHASES.md`)
13	
14	1. User can create / edit / save drill profiles.
15	2. Configurable per-profile: cue type set, delay range, late threshold,
16	   hesitation threshold, response window, scoring weights, round structure,
17	   distance axis on/off.
18	3. Hesitation detection uses an explicit, configurable RT band.
19	4. Choice-RT defaults: hesitation > 450 ms, late > 600 ms (tunable).
20	5. Per-cue-type RT and error-rate breakdown in the session summary.
2
